hat since most of the errands are dead  or joined the faith the heir to the Vale  after Robert is Harold Harding Robert's  father's sister's daughter's son  Littlefinger plans to marry Sansa to  Harold in order to win power over both  the Vale and the north though in the  show Sansa is married to Ramsay Bolton  which is kind of a crazier plan anyway  Harald or Harry is believed to be the  heir to the  bail but Littlefinger mentions that one  of Harry's mother's older sisters was  carried off by the burned men if that  unnamed waynwood happened to have a  legitimate child with one of the burned  men that child would be the heir to the  Vale ahead of Harry fan speculate that  Timur the only named burned man in the  story is that child the rightful Lord of  the Vale after Robert admittedly we're  not given any evidence that this  waynwood woman ever had a son with the  burned men but it's certainly plausible  and it could make a lot of narrative  sense for the mountain clans to take  control of the veil because Tyrion  promises the veil to the Klansmen and we  are all told this cousin Lannister  always pays her debts Lannister always  pays his debts Lannister always pays his  debts and Tyrion is currently working  with Daenerys Targaryen who intends to  eventually invade Westeros many fans  believe that the Vale could be an  important location in Daenerys invasion  because of its huge mountaintop Castle  the IRA which is considered impregnable  unless you have dragons  Daenerys could fly right up there on  drag on so if Daenerys does invade the  Vale it would make a lot of sense to  used here in relationship with the  mountain clans to help take it  in fact Tyrion has already mentioned a  plan to use the clans against the Vale  also we're told that the clansmen  especially timid and the burned man have  become bolder and more powerful since  returning from King's Landing so there's  little doubt that be keen for an attack  so the pace is a role here for Tyrion to  use 